A||N||5||terryk||Ryane coilover uncompressed spring height?||||1||
Z||000000||terryk||10-11-2001||03:46 PM||||Anyone know what the uncompressed spring height was of the Ryane coilover kit? I need to buy a set of #300 springs and need the length.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||10-11-2001||04:06 PM||||I believe there are several different lengths......8", 10" & 12".  <P>I remember talking with the Held Motorsports guys at the Fiero Factory swap meet this year and was told there were various lengths to choose from.<P>Go to <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.heldmotorsports.com</A>   maybe they list lengths there?<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||10-11-2001||04:17 PM||||The ones they sent me were 12".||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||10-11-2001||05:07 PM||||I suspected 12". Interesting.<P>I wonder how they determined which one's to send with the stock kit.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||10-11-2001||07:25 PM||||The threaded sleeves from Ryane were 7 " long, so there was about 6.5" of adjustment. They slid all the way to the bottom of the strut tube against the lower mount. I'm sure you could go with 10" if you want the car to sit a bit lower. My perches were about midway on the sleeves with 12" springs, but that was with the Lambo body and 305/50/15 tires so I don't know if it sat lower than stock or not. I think it was pretty close to stock ride height. If you're using a 5" sleeve, you may need 12" springs to get stock ride height.||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||10-11-2001||08:00 PM||||Since you mention it, it's going on a Lambo kit. Right now it looks like a 4WD. It needs to come down about 5" but we can't get the from down that much (drop spindles or springs) so we are settling for 3"-ish.||||reg||1
